  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SustainBrew - Empowering Indonesia&apos;s Coffee Communities and Promoting Social Sustainability in Indonesia&apos;s Coffee Value Chain</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The initiative led by Sucafina, JDE Peet&#x2019;s, CARE Indonesia, and CARE Netherlands is set to address social sustainability challenges within Java&apos;s coffee supply chain, with a strong focus on improving working conditions, enhancing financial stability, and boosting the involvement of women and youth.Beginning with a comprehensive baseline study, the project seeks to grasp the local context through direct engagement with coffee farmers, cooperatives, intermediaries, and grassroots organizations. This essential groundwork enables the development of an inclusive action plan through collaborative workshops involving key stakeholders such as local government officials, coffee cooperatives, community leaders, and representatives from both coffee farmer groups and women &amp; youth coffee farmer groups. These collaborative efforts aim to co-create and refine the action plan, ensuring it reflects a wide array of community perspectives.</narrative>
  </description>
